      content="When you pull up to a landscape supply depot or sand quarry, ask specifically for 'Washed Concrete Sand' or 'ASTM C33 Torpedo Sand.' Take a handful and rub it between your fingers. It should feel gritty and coarse, like sharp brown sugar with tiny 1/8-inch pebbles mixed in. If it feels silky, powdery, or leaves white dust on your palms, you have been given masonry sand or stone dust—reject the load immediately."
